The attached image, Figure 5, demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A shows flow cytometry dot plots, indicating a marked increase in both OVA and Nano-11 fluorescence when BMDCs are incubated with the Nano-11+OVA complex compared to cells treated with either component alone. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, quantifies this, showing a significant shift in the mean fluorescence intensity for BMDCs exposed to Nano-11+OVA, confirming that Nano-11 facilitates greater antigen internalization. These results highlight Nano-11's ability to enhance antigen delivery to DCs, a critical step in immune activation.